// @no-instantiate
// MISCOMPILE, pinned: a `Circle[]` ref-list ELEMENT resolves its heap type through the
// STRUCT table whenever a LAYOUT TWIN of the element type exists, instead of through the
// list's own element identity. `vl check` exits 0 (four redundant-annotation hints, nothing
// above HINT) and is the ONLY command that misses it — `vl check --codegen` exits 1,
// `vl build` writes the `.wasm` and exits 1, `vl run` exits 1. The engine refuses the module:
//
//   the emitted module is not valid wasm … type mismatch:
//   expected (ref null $type), found (ref $type)   (at offset 0x15c)
//
// `Dot` and `Circle` have identical layout (`{ r: i32 }`), and `Circle` is also a member of
// the union `Shape` — so it has a row in the VARIANT namespace as well. With a layout twin
// present in `sNames` the element read resolves through the struct table and picks the twin's
// row; with no twin it resolves through `uVarHeap` and is right.
//
// CONTROLS, all of which RUN: the same file with `Dot` DELETED; the same file with
// `type Dot = { d: i32 }` (a struct that is NOT a layout twin); and the same `Circle` value
// not put in a list (`return c.r` in place of the two list lines).
//
// AND THE TWIN DOES NOT HAVE TO BE THE CALLER'S OWN TYPE — one `std:array` `reduce` at a
// union accumulator mints it, which is the spelling a user meets. That variant is in the row.
//
// It is `silent-class-inventory.md` D32, filed 2026-08-26 while closing D26 and NOT a
// regression: identical on master (`c99838a8`, `7fe81e5b`, `a80c6717`) and on D26's branch,
// same 16 cells of D26's own 240-cell grid, same message. It is the seam ROADMAP charters as
// repOf item (e).
//
// IT REPLACED the D30 specimen (`xfail-miscompile-map-return-if-arm-tail-caller.vl`), which
// was deleted when D30 closed — `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts` had already NAMED this row as
// the successor rather than leaving it to be re-derived, and this file is that instruction
// carried out. WHEN IT IS FIXED this file starts failing (the module instantiates), which is
// the point: delete it, graduate a `@run` row, and swap `INVALID_MODULE_SRC` for another live
// member of the class.
//
// READ THE NOTE IN `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts` BEFORE DOING THAT. D30 and D32 were the
// last two live rows in `silent-class-inventory.md`, and they were closed in parallel. If D32
// closes there may be NO live member of the class left to name, and the question of what
// should guard that test then is an open one — not something to answer by weakening the
// assertion.
// @hint redundant type annotation: `useShape` is inferred as `i32`
// @hint redundant type annotation: `circleList` is inferred as `i32`
// @hint redundant type annotation: `c` is inferred as `{r: i32}`
// @hint redundant type annotation: `xs` is inferred as `Circle[]`
type Dot = { r: i32 }
type Circle = { r: i32 }
type Sq = { s: i32 }
type Shape = Circle | Sq

function mkD(): Dot { return { r: 3 } }

function useShape(): i32 {
  const s: Shape = { r: 1 }
  if s is Circle { return s.r }
  return -2
}

function circleList(): i32 {
  const c: Circle = { r: 8 }
  const xs: Circle[] = [c]
  return xs[0].r
}

print(circleList())
print(useShape())
print(mkD().r)
